[{"category":"section","location":"#ConstrainedDFO.jl","page":"ConstrainedDFO.jl","text":"","title":"ConstrainedDFO.jl"},{"category":"type","location":"#ConstrainedDFO.EqualityManifold","page":"ConstrainedDFO.jl","text":"EqualityManifold <: AbstractManifold{ℝ}\n\nA smooth Riemannian submanifold of mathbbR^n defined as the set\n\n    mathcalM=leftxinmathbbR^n  h(x)=0right\n\nfor some smooth function h mathbbR^ntomathbbR such that nabla h(x) has full rank for all xinmathcalM.\n\nFields\n\ndefining_function: the function h as described above.\ndimension: the dimension of the manifold, defined as the common dimension of its tangent spaces.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ConstrainedDFO.EqualityManifold"},{"category":"type","location":"#ConstrainedDFO.NOverSpectral","page":"ConstrainedDFO.jl","text":"Computes a lower bound to the invertibility radius as\n\n\\frac{n}{\\max\\{\\lambda(\n\nabla^2 h_i(x)) : i\\in{1,...,p}}}.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ConstrainedDFO.NOverSpectral"},{"category":"type","location":"#ConstrainedDFO.NOverSqrtSpectral","page":"ConstrainedDFO.jl","text":"Computes a lower bound to the invertibility radius as\n\n\\frac{n}{\\sqrt{\\max\\{\\lambda(\n\nabla^2 h_i(x)) : i\\in{1,...,p}}}}.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ConstrainedDFO.NOverSqrtSpectral"},{"category":"type","location":"#ConstrainedDFO.OneOverSpectral","page":"ConstrainedDFO.jl","text":"OneOverSpectral <: AbstractInvertibilityBound\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ConstrainedDFO.OneOverSpectral"},{"category":"type","location":"#ConstrainedDFO.OneOverSqrtSpectral","page":"ConstrainedDFO.jl","text":"Computes a lower bound to the invertibility radius as\n\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\max\\{\\lambda(\n\nabla^2 h_i(x)) : i\\in{1,...,p}}}}.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ConstrainedDFO.OneOverSqrtSpectral"},{"category":"type","location":"#ConstrainedDFO.RDFOState","page":"ConstrainedDFO.jl","text":"Fields\n\np is the current iterate on the manifold.\nd is the current best tangent vector found at T_pmathcalM.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ConstrainedDFO.RDFOState"},{"category":"type","location":"#ConstrainedDFO.StopAfterEvaluation","page":"ConstrainedDFO.jl","text":"StopAfterEvaluation <: DFStoppingCriterion\n\nA functor for a stopping criterion to stop after a maximal number of blackbox evaluations. Fields and constructor are the same as StopAfterIteration.\n\nTODO.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ConstrainedDFO.StopAfterEvaluation"},{"category":"method","location":"#ConstrainedDFO.get_eval_budget-Tuple{ConstrainedDFO.DefaultEvalManager}","page":"ConstrainedDFO.jl","text":"get_eval_budget(em::AbstractEvalManager)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ConstrainedDFO.get_eval_budget"},{"category":"method","location":"#ConstrainedDFO.invertibility_radius-Tuple{EqualityManifold, Any, ManifoldsBase.ProjectionRetraction, OneOverSpectral}","page":"ConstrainedDFO.jl","text":"invertibility_radius(M::EqualityManifold, p, m::ProjectionRetraction, b::OneOverSpectral)\n\nReturn a lower bound on the invertibility_radius of the ProjectionRetraction as\n\n    frac1maxlambda(H_h_i(x))  iin1p\n\nwhere H_h_i is the Hessian matrix of the defining subfunction h_i for M.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ConstrainedDFO.invertibility_radius"},{"category":"method","location":"#ConstrainedDFO.invertibility_radius-Tuple{EqualityManifold, Any}","page":"ConstrainedDFO.jl","text":"TODO. Document here.\nThis function precisely returns an artificial lower bound.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ConstrainedDFO.invertibility_radius"},{"category":"method","location":"#ConstrainedDFO.invertibility_radius-Tuple{ManifoldsBase.AbstractManifold, Any}","page":"ConstrainedDFO.jl","text":"invertibility_radius(M, p; m, b)\n\nTODO.\nWrite the doc that describes this as a lower bound on the radius where the retraction is supposed to be invertible.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ConstrainedDFO.invertibility_radius"},{"category":"method","location":"#ConstrainedDFO.latin_hypercube_sampling-Tuple{Int64, Vector{Float64}, Vector{Float64}, Int64}","page":"ConstrainedDFO.jl","text":"latin_hypercube_sampling(n, lb, ub, p)\n\nPerform a latin hypercube sampling with given bounds, and return p sampled points. It is assumed that bounds are well-defined.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ConstrainedDFO.latin_hypercube_sampling"},{"category":"method","location":"#ConstrainedDFO.solve_problem-Tuple{AbstractDFSolver, ConstrainedDFO.AbstractBenchmarkProblem}","page":"ConstrainedDFO.jl","text":"Test\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ConstrainedDFO.solve_problem"},{"category":"method","location":"#ConstrainedDFO.update_remaining_evals!-Tuple{ConstrainedDFO.DefaultEvalManager, Int64}","page":"ConstrainedDFO.jl","text":"update_remaining_evals(dem::DefaultEvalManager)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ConstrainedDFO.update_remaining_evals!"}]
